# See doc at https://raw.githubusercontent.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/master/prdoc/schema_user.json

title: 'sc-dkg: aggregatable DKG gadget over BEEFY BLS keys (prototype)'

doc:
  - audience: Node Dev
    description: |
      Adds `sc-dkg`, a prototype gadget for an aggregatable distributed key generation
      (a-DKG, `adkg-vrf`) among relay-chain validators that reuses their paired
      ECDSA,BLS12-381 BEEFY keys (read from `Beefy::NextAuthorities`). In every session
      the validator deals, gossips signed dealings with session-scoped validation, and
      submits its own dealing over JSON-RPC to a parachain that aggregates the dealings
      into a per-session threshold key (`sc_dkg::submit::rpc_dealing_submitter`, which
      validates before submitting so an early dealing is not banned by the pool).
      Experimental: test-network only, not wired into the polkadot binary.

      `PolkadotServiceBuilder` gains `notification_metrics`, `peer_store_handle`,
      `keystore` and `add_extra_notification_protocol`, so an embedder can run an
      additional gossip gadget on the relay-chain node.

crates:
  - name: sc-dkg
    bump: major
  - name: polkadot-service
    bump: minor
